      "writtenOn": "2026-10-26T19:44:06Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "To be honest, I think modifying the core/bpf code is a non starter.\n\nThat being said, I did a bit of digging with jetski with regards to @aliceryhl@google.com\u0027s comments about FD manipulation and I think what actually matters is as follows:\n1. the loader data must be the exact bytes the kernel read from the verified ELF when the loader program is verified and run, and\n2. the loader program that runs must be the one the kernel loaded, bound to that data.\n\nI think we can mitigate Alice\u0027s concern without changing the core BPF code by pinning the associated objects, setting BPF_MAP_FREEZE on the loader map before populating it in the kernel, and verify as follows:\n\n\n```\n    /* drivers/android/bpf/bpf_fd_loader_run.c  (or inline in the Rust driver via bindings) */\n    int bpf_fd_loader_run(const void *insns, u32 insn_cnt, const void *data, u32 data_sz,\n    \t\t      const char *license, void *kctx, u32 ctx_sz)\n    {\n    \tunion bpf_attr attr;\n    \tstruct bpf_map *map;\n    \tstruct bpf_prog *prog;\n    \tint map_fd, prog_fd, err;\n    \tu32 key \u003d 0;\n\n    \t/* 1. create loader map (fd + id are allocated, that\u0027s fine) */\n    \tmemset(\u0026attr, 0, sizeof(attr));\n    \tattr.map_type \u003d BPF_MAP_TYPE_ARRAY; attr.key_size \u003d 4;\n    \tattr.value_size \u003d data_sz; attr.max_entries \u003d 1;\n    \tstrscpy(attr.map_name, \"__loader.map\", sizeof(attr.map_name));\n    \tmap_fd \u003d kern_sys_bpf(BPF_MAP_CREATE, \u0026attr, sizeof(attr));\n    \tif (map_fd \u003c 0) return map_fd;\n\n    \t/* pin the object we actually created, independent of what fd N points to later */\n    \tmap \u003d bpf_map_get(map_fd);\n    \tif (IS_ERR(map)) { err \u003d PTR_ERR(map); goto close_map_fd; }\n\n    \t/* 2. FREEZE FIRST, then populate from the kernel side.\n    \t *    After freeze, no fd (dup\u0027d or GET_FD_BY_ID) can write: map_get_sys_perms()\n    \t *    strips FMODE_CAN_WRITE and writable mmap is refused. The direct ops call\n    \t *    below is the kernel\u0027s own write path and is not gated by -\u003efrozen.\n    \t */\n    \tmemset(\u0026attr, 0, sizeof(attr)); attr.map_fd \u003d map_fd;\n    \terr \u003d kern_sys_bpf(BPF_MAP_FREEZE, \u0026attr, sizeof(attr));\n    \tif (err) goto put_map;\n    \tif (!READ_ONCE(map-\u003efrozen)) { err \u003d -EAGAIN; goto put_map; } /* fd N was swapped */\n\n    \terr \u003d map-\u003eops-\u003emap_update_elem(map, \u0026key, (void *)data, 0);\n    \tif (err) goto put_map;\n\n    \t/* 3. load loader prog; fd_array resolves fd N at verification time */\n    \tmemset(\u0026attr, 0, sizeof(attr));\n    \tattr.prog_type \u003d BPF_PROG_TYPE_SYSCALL;\n    \tattr.insns \u003d (long)insns; attr.insn_cnt \u003d insn_cnt;\n    \tattr.license \u003d (long)license;\n    \tattr.fd_array \u003d (long)\u0026map_fd;\n    \tattr.prog_flags \u003d BPF_F_SLEEPABLE;\n    \t/* optional: forward log_level/log_size/log_buf from struct bpf_loader_ctx header */\n    \tstrscpy(attr.prog_name, \"__loader.prog\", sizeof(attr.prog_name));\n    \tprog_fd \u003d kern_sys_bpf(BPF_PROG_LOAD, \u0026attr, sizeof(attr));\n    \tif (prog_fd \u003c 0) { err \u003d prog_fd; goto put_map; }\n\n    \tprog \u003d bpf_prog_get_type_dev(prog_fd, BPF_PROG_TYPE_SYSCALL, false);\n    \tif (IS_ERR(prog)) { err \u003d PTR_ERR(prog); goto close_prog_fd; }\n\n    \t/* binding check: the prog we hold must use exactly the map we hold.\n    \t * If fd N was swapped before/while the verifier resolved fd_array, this fails.\n    \t */\n    \tif (prog-\u003eaux-\u003eused_map_cnt !\u003d 1 || prog-\u003eaux-\u003eused_maps[0] !\u003d map) {\n    \t\terr \u003d -EAGAIN; goto put_prog;\n    \t}\n    \tif (ctx_sz \u003c prog-\u003eaux-\u003emax_ctx_offset) { err \u003d -EINVAL; goto put_prog; }\n\n    \t/* 4. run — on the pinned object, no fd involved */\n    \trcu_read_lock_trace();\n    \terr \u003d (int)bpf_prog_run_pin_on_cpu(prog, kctx);   /* inline in \u003clinux/filter.h\u003e */\n    \trcu_read_unlock_trace();\n    \tif (err \u003c 0 \u0026\u0026 !IS_ERR_VALUE((long)err)) err \u003d -EINVAL;\n    \tif (err \u003e 0) err \u003d 0;\n\n    put_prog:\n    \tbpf_prog_put(prog);\n    close_prog_fd:\n    \tclose_fd(prog_fd);\n    put_map:\n    \tbpf_map_put(map);\n    close_map_fd:\n    \tclose_fd(map_fd);\n    \treturn err;\n    }\n```\n\nThoughts?",
